---
/**
 * Track 8 (Visual Math: Calculus), Lesson 8, illustration.
 *
 * Implicit differentiation, made geometric. The circle x^2 + y^2 = 25
 * (radius 5, centered at the origin) is drawn on x-y axes. The point
 * (3, 4) sits on the circle: 9 + 16 = 25. From the origin to that point
 * we draw the RADIUS, whose slope is rise over run, 4/3. At the point we
 * draw the TANGENT line, whose slope is -3/4.
 *
 * Differentiating x^2 + y^2 = 25 implicitly gives 2x + 2y(dy/dx) = 0, so
 * dy/dx = -x/y. At (3, 4) that is -3/4, the negative reciprocal of the
 * radius slope 4/3. Negative-reciprocal slopes are perpendicular, so the
 * tangent meets the radius at a right angle, marked with a small square.
 */

const cx = 250; // pixel x of the math origin (0, 0)
const cy = 180; // pixel y of the math origin (0, 0)
const SCALE = 22; // pixels per math unit; range [-6, 6] spans 132 px each side

// math (x, y) -> pixel (px, py), with y flipped so math-up is pixel-up
const px = (mx: number) => cx + mx * SCALE;
const py = (my: number) => cy - my * SCALE;

const R = 5; // circle radius in math units
const AX = 6; // axis half-extent in math units

// the point on the circle
const PX_MATH = 3;
const PY_MATH = 4;

// tangent slope is -3/4; draw the tangent as a segment around the point
const TAN_SLOPE = -3 / 4;
const TAN_HALF = 4.4; // half-length of the tangent segment in x math units
const tanX1 = PX_MATH - TAN_HALF;
const tanY1 = PY_MATH + TAN_SLOPE * (tanX1 - PX_MATH);
const tanX2 = PX_MATH + TAN_HALF;
const tanY2 = PY_MATH + TAN_SLOPE * (tanX2 - PX_MATH);

// right-angle square at (3, 4): unit step inward along the radius and along
// the tangent, both in math units. Radius direction (origin -> point) is
// (3, 4)/5; tangent direction is (4, -3)/5 (perpendicular, unit length).
const SQ = 0.7; // square side in math units
const radDir = { x: -PX_MATH / 5, y: -PY_MATH / 5 }; // from point back toward origin
const tanDir = { x: 4 / 5, y: -3 / 5 }; // along the tangent
const sqA = { x: PX_MATH, y: PY_MATH };
const sqB = { x: PX_MATH + radDir.x * SQ, y: PY_MATH + radDir.y * SQ };
const sqC = { x: sqB.x + tanDir.x * SQ, y: sqB.y + tanDir.y * SQ };
const sqD = { x: PX_MATH + tanDir.x * SQ, y: PY_MATH + tanDir.y * SQ };

// circle path sample points
const N_CIRCLE = 96;

// axis ticks (skip 0)
const ticks = [-5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5];

const TEAL = '#0d9488';
const AMBER = '#d97706';
const ACCENT = '#7c3aed';
const SKY = '#0284c7';
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 720 360" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="ca-impl-title ca-impl-desc">
		<title id="ca-impl-title">The circle x squared plus y squared equals 25 with the radius to (3, 4) of slope 4/3 perpendicular to the tangent line of slope minus 3/4</title>
		<desc id="ca-impl-desc">A coordinate plane with x and y axes through the origin. The circle of radius 5 centered at the origin, the graph of x squared plus y squared equals 25, is drawn in sky blue. The point (3, 4) is marked on the circle in the upper right. A radius line in amber runs from the origin to (3, 4); its slope is rise over run, 4 over 3. A tangent line to the circle at (3, 4), highlighted in accent purple, has slope minus 3 over 4. A small square at (3, 4) marks the right angle between the radius and the tangent, showing they are perpendicular. Implicit differentiation of x squared plus y squared equals 25 gives dy/dx equals minus x over y, which is minus 3 over 4 at this point, the negative reciprocal of the radius slope.</desc>

		<defs>
			<marker id="ca-impl-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
				<path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="currentColor" />
			</marker>
		</defs>

		{/* axes */}
		<line x1={px(-AX)} y1={cy} x2={px(AX) + 6} y2={cy} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.55" marker-end="url(#ca-impl-arrow)" />
		<line x1={cx} y1={py(-AX)} x2={cx} y2={py(AX) - 6} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.55" marker-end="url(#ca-impl-arrow)" />

		{/* axis tick marks */}
		{ticks.map((t) => (
			<g>
				<line x1={px(t)} y1={cy - 3} x2={px(t)} y2={cy + 3} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.45" />
				<line x1={cx - 3} y1={py(t)} x2={cx + 3} y2={py(t)} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.45" />
			</g>
		))}

		{/* axis labels */}
		<text x={px(AX) + 10} y={cy + 4} text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">x</text>
		<text x={cx + 6} y={py(AX) - 8} text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">y</text>

		{/* the circle x^2 + y^2 = 25, sampled as a polyline */}
		<path
			d={Array.from({ length: N_CIRCLE + 1 }, (_, i) => {
				const a = (i / N_CIRCLE) * 2 * Math.PI;
				const mx = R * Math.cos(a);
				const my = R * Math.sin(a);
				return `${i === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'} ${px(mx).toFixed(2)} ${py(my).toFixed(2)}`;
			}).join(' ')}
			fill={SKY}
			fill-opacity="0.05"
			stroke={SKY}
			stroke-width="2"
		/>

		{/* radius line from origin to (3, 4) */}
		<line x1={cx} y1={cy} x2={px(PX_MATH)} y2={py(PY_MATH)} stroke={AMBER} stroke-width="2.4" />

		{/* tangent line at (3, 4), highlighted */}
		<line x1={px(tanX1)} y1={py(tanY1)} x2={px(tanX2)} y2={py(tanY2)} stroke={ACCENT} stroke-width="2.6" />

		{/* right-angle square at (3, 4) */}
		<path
			d={`M ${px(sqA.x).toFixed(2)} ${py(sqA.y).toFixed(2)} L ${px(sqB.x).toFixed(2)} ${py(sqB.y).toFixed(2)} L ${px(sqC.x).toFixed(2)} ${py(sqC.y).toFixed(2)} L ${px(sqD.x).toFixed(2)} ${py(sqD.y).toFixed(2)} Z`}
			fill="none"
			stroke="currentColor"
			stroke-width="1.3"
			opacity="0.8"
		/>

		{/* the point (3, 4) */}
		<circle cx={px(PX_MATH)} cy={py(PY_MATH)} r="4.5" fill={ACCENT} stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.2" />
		<text x={px(PX_MATH) + 12} y={py(PY_MATH) - 8} text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>(3, 4)</text>

		{/* origin dot */}
		<circle cx={cx} cy={cy} r="2.6" fill="currentColor" />

		{/* radius slope label, near the middle of the radius */}
		<text x={px(PX_MATH / 2) - 10} y={py(PY_MATH / 2) - 6} text-anchor="end" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill={AMBER}>slope 4/3</text>

		{/* tangent slope label, near the upper-left end of the tangent */}
		<text x={px(tanX1) + 6} y={py(tanY1) - 8} text-anchor="start" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>slope -3/4</text>

		{/* legend: implicit differentiation result */}
		<g transform="translate(486, 232)">
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="220" height="104" rx="6" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.04" />
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="220" height="104" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.3" />
			<text x="110" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">differentiate implicitly:</text>
			<text x="110" y="44" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">2x + 2y·(dy/dx) = 0</text>
			<text x="110" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>dy/dx = -x/y = -3/4</text>
			<text x="110" y="90" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">negative reciprocal of 4/3</text>
		</g>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>The circle x² + y² = 25 has radius 5, so the point (3, 4) lies on it (9 + 16 = 25). The radius from the origin to (3, 4) climbs 4 for every 3 across, a slope of 4/3. Differentiating x² + y² = 25 implicitly gives 2x + 2y·(dy/dx) = 0, so dy/dx = -x/y, which equals -3/4 at (3, 4). That tangent slope is the negative reciprocal of the radius slope 4/3, which is exactly the condition for the radius and the tangent to be perpendicular. The small square at (3, 4) marks that right angle.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus { margin: 1.75rem auto; max-width: 100%; }
	.cw-illus svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 720px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
	.cw-illus figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic; }
</style>
